Module walk "The Walk of the Milestones" {

  // ---- The Brethren: the Walk's hard edge. Brother Gaunt and his three staves come to the host on the eighth day and take the
  // Station of the Gathering town for a sanctuary; they let pass whoever speaks the names, and fight whoever comes armed.
  Person gaunt "Someone" nowhere {
    Role "the Stave-Master of the Brethren, who holds the Station". Calling warrior. Level 4. Temperament defensive. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Warns "The man at the Station arch has not moved since you came in sight; his staff is planted like a pole in a flag-bearer's hand. 'Names,' says {gaunt}. 'Not yours. The road's. Say one and pass. Say none and turn.' The three behind him have lowered their staves an inch, each, as one.".
    Comes "{gaunt} does not shout. He says a word, which is a number, and the staves come down in a row.".
    Pleads "{gaunt} sits down on the Station step with his staff across his knees, and breathes, and looks at the stone. 'The road is not held,' he says, 'by this arm. Remember that I said it.'".
    Lair station_b.
  }
  Person staves "the Stave-Brethren" nowhere {
    Role "three of the Brethren, in sacking, with staves of ash shod in iron". Calling warrior. Numbers 3. Level 2. Temperament defensive. Manner grim.
    Lair station_b.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp(gaunt) to 400.
  Initially Set encounterXp(staves) to 150.
  Person hask "Someone" nowhere {
    Role "a sergeant of the Marcher's horse, who has been asked to see the Hundred quiet". Calling warrior. Level 5. Temperament territorial. Manner stoic. Pronouns he.
    Warns "The sergeant sits his horse as if it were furniture. 'We have been asked to see the Hundred quiet,' says {hask}, courteously. 'I have a price for that, and it is not money. It is that you are not here when the courtesy stops.' He looks past you at what is behind you. 'I do not like what I count.' The three behind him have not drawn, and the way they sit says it is a matter of time and not of intention.".
    Comes "{hask} says one word, and it is not loud. The horsemen come on at a walk, which is worse.".
    Pleads "{hask} puts up a hand, and his men stop. 'That will do,' he says. 'I was not told there would be anyone.'".
    Lair green_b.
  }
  Person riders "the Marcher's riders" nowhere {
    Role "three riders in dark leather, mounted, with short spears". Calling warrior. Numbers 3. Level 3. Temperament territorial. Manner stoic.
    Lair green_b.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp(hask) to 500.
  Initially Set encounterXp(riders) to 250.
  Person mob "the crowd" nowhere {
    Role "a crowd in the green's dust, that was a Walk at breakfast". Calling commoner. Numbers 6. Level 1. Temperament savage. Manner grim.
    Comes "The crowd turns, all at once, with the single face a crowd has: staves, stones, the dull light in the eyes. It is not that they know you. It is that you are in the way.".
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp(mob) to 120.
  Rule gaunt_comes_b when flashpoint(f_b) and day(clock) >= 8 and not gaunt_here(walk) and at(gaunt, ?a) and at(staves, ?b) { Retract at(gaunt, ?a). Assert at(gaunt, station_b). Retract at(staves, ?b). Assert at(staves, station_b). Assert lair(gaunt, station_b). Assert lair(staves, station_b). Assert gaunt_here(walk). }
  Rule hask_comes_b when flashpoint(f_b) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 12 and not hask_here(walk) and at(hask, ?a) and at(riders, ?b) { Retract at(hask, ?a). Assert at(hask, green_b). Retract at(riders, ?b). Assert at(riders, green_b). Assert lair(hask, green_b). Assert lair(riders, green_b). Assert hask_here(walk). }
  Rule hask_goes_b when flashpoint(f_b) and hask_here(walk) and raid_off(walk) and not raid_done(walk) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 22 and not decided(walk) { Assert raid_done(walk). Assert tolerates(hask, party). Assert tolerates(riders, party). }
  Rule raid_b heard at camp_b when flashpoint(f_b) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 22 and hask_here(walk) and not raid_off(walk) and not raid_done(walk) and not state(gate_bar_b, dropped) and at(hask, ?a) and at(riders, ?b)
    says "Horses on the road in the dark, many, walking. The camp's fires go down one by one as people see them; somebody tries to rouse the lads, who have fallen asleep in a heap. Then the gate-posts are lit from behind by torches, and a man's voice says, quite quietly, 'In the Bench's name.'" { Retract at(hask, ?a). Assert at(hask, camp_b). Retract at(riders, ?b). Assert at(riders, camp_b). Assert raided(walk). Assert raid_done(walk). }
  Rule raid_barred_b heard at green_b when flashpoint(f_b) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 22 and hask_here(walk) and not raid_off(walk) and not raid_done(walk) and state(gate_bar_b, dropped)
    says "Horses in the dark on the green, many, and torches. The camp gate is barred from inside; the walkers behind it are singing, not loudly. The sergeant sits his horse before the bar until the lamps go out, and does not give the word." { Assert gate_held(walk). Assert raid_done(walk). }
  Rule lads_bar_b when flashpoint(f_b) and lads_allied(walk) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 21 and not state(gate_bar_b, dropped) and not raid_done(walk) and not decided(walk) says "Rhys comes tearing across the camp with his shirt out. 'Horses! On the common! Lots of them! Cal says they are the Bench's, and Cal is wrong about everything, but I thought I would bar the gate anyway, just in case. It is barred.' It is, with an ash pole and a bucket of stones against it, and an expression of great pride." teaches riders_known { Assert state(gate_bar_b, dropped). }
  Rule gaunt_comes_c when flashpoint(f_c) and day(clock) >= 8 and not gaunt_here(walk) and at(gaunt, ?a) and at(staves, ?b) { Retract at(gaunt, ?a). Assert at(gaunt, station_c). Retract at(staves, ?b). Assert at(staves, station_c). Assert lair(gaunt, station_c). Assert lair(staves, station_c). Assert gaunt_here(walk). }
  Rule hask_comes_c when flashpoint(f_c) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 12 and not hask_here(walk) and at(hask, ?a) and at(riders, ?b) { Retract at(hask, ?a). Assert at(hask, green_c). Retract at(riders, ?b). Assert at(riders, green_c). Assert lair(hask, green_c). Assert lair(riders, green_c). Assert hask_here(walk). }
  Rule hask_goes_c when flashpoint(f_c) and hask_here(walk) and raid_off(walk) and not raid_done(walk) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 22 and not decided(walk) { Assert raid_done(walk). Assert tolerates(hask, party). Assert tolerates(riders, party). }
  Rule raid_c heard at camp_c when flashpoint(f_c) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 22 and hask_here(walk) and not raid_off(walk) and not raid_done(walk) and not state(gate_bar_c, dropped) and at(hask, ?a) and at(riders, ?b)
    says "Horses on the road in the dark, many, walking. The camp's fires go down one by one as people see them; somebody tries to rouse the lads, who have fallen asleep in a heap. Then the gate-posts are lit from behind by torches, and a man's voice says, quite quietly, 'In the Bench's name.'" { Retract at(hask, ?a). Assert at(hask, camp_c). Retract at(riders, ?b). Assert at(riders, camp_c). Assert raided(walk). Assert raid_done(walk). }
  Rule raid_barred_c heard at green_c when flashpoint(f_c) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 22 and hask_here(walk) and not raid_off(walk) and not raid_done(walk) and state(gate_bar_c, dropped)
    says "Horses in the dark on the green, many, and torches. The camp gate is barred from inside; the walkers behind it are singing, not loudly. The sergeant sits his horse before the bar until the lamps go out, and does not give the word." { Assert gate_held(walk). Assert raid_done(walk). }
  Rule lads_bar_c when flashpoint(f_c) and lads_allied(walk) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 21 and not state(gate_bar_c, dropped) and not raid_done(walk) and not decided(walk) says "Rhys comes tearing across the camp with his shirt out. 'Horses! On the common! Lots of them! Cal says they are the Bench's, and Cal is wrong about everything, but I thought I would bar the gate anyway, just in case. It is barred.' It is, with an ash pole and a bucket of stones against it, and an expression of great pride." teaches riders_known { Assert state(gate_bar_c, dropped). }
  Rule gaunt_comes_d when flashpoint(f_d) and day(clock) >= 8 and not gaunt_here(walk) and at(gaunt, ?a) and at(staves, ?b) { Retract at(gaunt, ?a). Assert at(gaunt, station_d). Retract at(staves, ?b). Assert at(staves, station_d). Assert lair(gaunt, station_d). Assert lair(staves, station_d). Assert gaunt_here(walk). }
  Rule hask_comes_d when flashpoint(f_d) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 12 and not hask_here(walk) and at(hask, ?a) and at(riders, ?b) { Retract at(hask, ?a). Assert at(hask, green_d). Retract at(riders, ?b). Assert at(riders, green_d). Assert lair(hask, green_d). Assert lair(riders, green_d). Assert hask_here(walk). }
  Rule hask_goes_d when flashpoint(f_d) and hask_here(walk) and raid_off(walk) and not raid_done(walk) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 22 and not decided(walk) { Assert raid_done(walk). Assert tolerates(hask, party). Assert tolerates(riders, party). }
  Rule raid_d heard at camp_d when flashpoint(f_d) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 22 and hask_here(walk) and not raid_off(walk) and not raid_done(walk) and not state(gate_bar_d, dropped) and at(hask, ?a) and at(riders, ?b)
    says "Horses on the road in the dark, many, walking. The camp's fires go down one by one as people see them; somebody tries to rouse the lads, who have fallen asleep in a heap. Then the gate-posts are lit from behind by torches, and a man's voice says, quite quietly, 'In the Bench's name.'" { Retract at(hask, ?a). Assert at(hask, camp_d). Retract at(riders, ?b). Assert at(riders, camp_d). Assert raided(walk). Assert raid_done(walk). }
  Rule raid_barred_d heard at green_d when flashpoint(f_d) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 22 and hask_here(walk) and not raid_off(walk) and not raid_done(walk) and state(gate_bar_d, dropped)
    says "Horses in the dark on the green, many, and torches. The camp gate is barred from inside; the walkers behind it are singing, not loudly. The sergeant sits his horse before the bar until the lamps go out, and does not give the word." { Assert gate_held(walk). Assert raid_done(walk). }
  Rule lads_bar_d when flashpoint(f_d) and lads_allied(walk) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 21 and not state(gate_bar_d, dropped) and not raid_done(walk) and not decided(walk) says "Rhys comes tearing across the camp with his shirt out. 'Horses! On the common! Lots of them! Cal says they are the Bench's, and Cal is wrong about everything, but I thought I would bar the gate anyway, just in case. It is barred.' It is, with an ash pole and a bucket of stones against it, and an expression of great pride." teaches riders_known { Assert state(gate_bar_d, dropped). }
  Relation gaunt_here(group). Relation hask_here(group). Relation raid_done(group). Relation raid_counted(group). Relation gaunt_counted(group). Relation interdict_counted(group). Relation flash_said(group).

  // ---- The ranger's tracks, the cause of the raid, and the drove-way round it.
  Observe riders_sign_b at green_b as sign noticed by woodcraft when flashpoint(f_b) and day(clock) >= 7 and day(clock) < 11 "In the dust beyond the last house: hoofmarks, heavy-shod, eight horses or nine, in from the north at night. They did not come into the town; they went round it by the common, and two of them waited at the old milestone, and one dismounted and stood a long time looking at the camp's ground. A troop, and not a market-party." teaches riders_known.
  Observe riders_horse_b at green_b as sign when flashpoint(f_b) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 12 and at(riders, green_b) "A string of dark horses stands on the common, hobbled, with dark leather over the saddle-bows, and a sergeant sitting his own as though it were a chair. Nobody on the green is looking at them, with the intensity of people who are not looking at them." teaches riders_known.
  Observe drove_b at green_b as sign noticed by woodcraft when flashpoint(f_b) and day(clock) >= 7 and day(clock) < 11 "A drove-way runs off the back of the green and round the hill, wide enough for sheep and a cart, and dry. It comes out on the high ground above the town a quarter-mile from the Station, where there is a spring and a wind-break of old oaks. A camp there could be seen from the Station and could not be got at in the dark.".
  Action drove_way_b(actor: group, site: place) "Lead the Walkers by the drove-way to the high ground, and camp them there" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, camp_b) and flashpoint(f_b) and capable(actor, woodcraft) and knows(actor, riders_known) and day(clock) == 9 and not round_led(walk) and not raid_done(walk).
    Time 120 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert round_led(walk). Assert raid_off(walk). }
    Result "It takes two hours and the Mile-Keeper's agreement, which is the harder of the two. By the time the sun is behind the hill the host is on the high ground with its fires lit behind the oaks, and the camp below is an empty square of trodden grass with a wheel with a wing on the gatepost. In the night, from above, you watch eleven torches go into the empty camp, and stay there, and come out again, slowly.".
    Otherwise "The drove-way is longer than it looked and the walkers are tired. Half of them are on it, and the rest are in the camp, and you have succeeded in making a division where there was none.".
  }
  Action bar_gate_hint_b(actor: group, site: place) "Show the walkers how to drop the camp gate's bar, and hold it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, camp_b) and flashpoint(f_b) and knows(actor, riders_known) and state(gate_bar_b, open) and day(clock) >= 9.
    Time 15 minutes.
    On success { Assert state(gate_bar_b, dropped). }
    Result "A pole of ash, two men, a notch in each post: the bar goes down and the gate is a wall. Nobody says what it is for, and everyone knows.".
  }
  Action pay_hask_b(actor: group, site: place) "Pay {hask} thirty crowns to be somewhere else tonight" {
    Speaker hask.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hask, site) and flashpoint(f_b) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 30 and not raid_off(walk).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 30. Assert raid_off(walk). Assert tolerates(hask, actor). Assert tolerates(riders, actor). }
    Result "'The Marcher's horse,' says {hask}, counting it with his thumb, 'is not for sale.' He pockets it. 'But my time is mine, and I find that tonight I have a great deal of it at the other end of the town. You will understand that I shall hear nothing, and that I do not know you.' He turns his horse. 'It is a pity. I should have liked to see what they were.'".
  }
  Action parley_hask_b(actor: group, site: place) "Ask {hask} to put his orders in writing before he carries them out" {
    Speaker hask.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hask, site) and flashpoint(f_b) and not raid_off(walk).
    Time 15 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert raid_off(walk). Assert tolerates(hask, actor). Assert tolerates(riders, actor). }
    Result "{hask} considers this for some time, with courtesy. 'There is no writing,' he says. 'There is the bailiff's word, which he has not given me yet, and a sergeant who has been told to wait for it.' A very small smile. 'I will wait for it until noon of the tenth. That is a thing I can do without any writing at all.'".
    Otherwise "{hask} hears you with the whole of his attention and then says, 'No,' with great kindness.".
  }
  Observe riders_sign_c at green_c as sign noticed by woodcraft when flashpoint(f_c) and day(clock) >= 7 and day(clock) < 11 "In the dust beyond the last house: hoofmarks, heavy-shod, eight horses or nine, in from the north at night. They did not come into the town; they went round it by the common, and two of them waited at the old milestone, and one dismounted and stood a long time looking at the camp's ground. A troop, and not a market-party." teaches riders_known.
  Observe riders_horse_c at green_c as sign when flashpoint(f_c) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 12 and at(riders, green_c) "A string of dark horses stands on the common, hobbled, with dark leather over the saddle-bows, and a sergeant sitting his own as though it were a chair. Nobody on the green is looking at them, with the intensity of people who are not looking at them." teaches riders_known.
  Observe drove_c at green_c as sign noticed by woodcraft when flashpoint(f_c) and day(clock) >= 7 and day(clock) < 11 "A drove-way runs off the back of the green and round the hill, wide enough for sheep and a cart, and dry. It comes out on the high ground above the town a quarter-mile from the Station, where there is a spring and a wind-break of old oaks. A camp there could be seen from the Station and could not be got at in the dark.".
